# Keep tracked SVG snapshots newline-stable across operating systems. render.py
# writes in the local text convention (CRLF on Windows), so without this a
# contributor running `python tests.py --update-samples` on Windows would
# commit CRLF churn. Git stores these as LF everywhere. The snapshot test
# compares with universal-newline reads, so it is unaffected either way.
*.svg text eol=lf
